seg-a2825327dc19 = Assess a real GNSS receiver log for trust: read a u-blox UBX, RINEX { "3" } (optionally with broadcast navigation, which adds the engine's own fix, RAIM and a clock-aided monitor), Android GnssLogger or NMEA log, run the trust monitors (carrier-to-noise density drop, AGC, jamming indicator, loss of lock, position jump, RAIM, clock) against a calibration baseline, and return when and why the receiver stopped being trustworthy. Optional <c1/> with onsets and predicted C/N0 drops are scored against tolerances stated in the scenario: detected, late or missed, and agree or disagree. Returns the summary and the full result JSON (chart and CSV on request; a vessel run's CSV begins with a <c2/> comment line carrying the advisory statement, which CSV readers skip with their comment option). The log's bytes go inline in the TOML as <c3/> or <c4/> (inline only, at most { "4" } MiB). A <c5/> table selects the maritime monitors (kinematic consistency, heading against course, speed log, antenna height, C/N0 spread, time consistency) and adds a 0-100 trust score per epoch with the monitors that deducted. Every epoch also carries its satellite <c6/> (good; degraded for few satellites or high PDOP or HDOP; or unknown where the log has no satellite elevations or DOP); every epoch has a <c7/> (good, fair, poor); for a vessel a <c8/> monitor joins the score, deducting only when the geometry is poor (at most { "15" } points: degraded, never untrusted), and every deduction carries a class: geometry (the sky), environment or inconsistency (attack-like). For a stream excerpt with the gate use <c9/>. Advisory only; evidence tier MODELLED.

