seg-7937ed00cbc0 = Sky geometry under an azimuth-dependent skyline (a street canyon, a harbour, a fjord, a container terminal): from a site, a time and constellation presets, two-line element sets (<c1/>, with a UTC <c2/>) or satellites given as azimuth/elevation or ECEF, which satellites are visible and which are hidden by the skyline, GDOP/PDOP/HDOP/VDOP/TDOP from the gnss_lib_py-checked DOP kernel, the east-north-up cofactor and covariance with one receiver clock per system (or one in common), and the horizontal error ellipse at one sigma and at a stated confidence for a stated UERE. With no <c3/>, describes a REPRESENTATIVE skyline preset with its provenance and its cut every degree (an empty <c4/> lists them). Scenarios of the orbit and integrity (with <c5/>), gnss-sim, jamming, leo-pvt and leo-pass kinds take the same <c6/> section through run_scenario. Evidence tier MODELLED: geometry under a stated error model, line of sight only; not a prediction of a receiver's real error and not an integrity bound; preset constellations are a representative sky, not the sky of a date; <c7/> text with an <c8/> (UTC) gives the sky those element sets give at that epoch (SGP4), not a measurement, and <c9/> says which. Carries the advisory: not type-approved navigation equipment. No Monte Carlo over MCP (bulk samples; use the CLI, Python or WASM). Inline only, at most { "4" } MiB.

